Lycia Player for Linux is a community Linux port fork of the
original Lycia Player (Windows-focused) by Billy636.

Upstream project:
https://github.com/Billy636/LyciaMusic

Fork notice:
- This repository is a modified version of the upstream work,
  redistributed under the same GNU Affero General Public License
  v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only), as required by the upstream license.
- Modifications carried by this fork (Linux platform adaptations,
  per AGPL-3.0 Section 5 "prominent notices" requirement):
  * Media controls via MPRIS/D-Bus (souvlaki) replacing Windows SMTC
  * Credential storage via Secret Service (keyring linux-native)
  * RPM bundle packaging support
  * Taskbar playback control degraded to a free floating widget
  * Asset protocol scope fix for covers under dotted directories
  * Automatic WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE under WSL (WSLg)
  * Update check endpoints repointed from the upstream release
    channels to this fork's GitHub Releases
- The original application, its logo, illustrations and screenshots
  remain copyrighted by the upstream authors. Windows users should
  prefer the upstream project.

